<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Harness.Loop</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Harness.Loop</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Build-plan 5.3 - the INNER LOOP, and nothing else.

    The pieces existed and nothing drove them in order: allocate the map, gate the submission, generate
    the copy layer, assert 0.1b, deploy, confirm the build, run the wave, package the results. This is
    that ordering and the handing-back.

    WHAT IT IS NOT: not the review skills (they exist), not the coordinator (phases 4 and 6), and not a
    verdict. *** THE LOOP NEVER DECIDES WHETHER A RESULT IS GOOD. *** DB-8 owns that, in a precedence
    the loop honours rather than re-derives - admissibility, then LIVENESS, then the run outcome, then
    settling, then CONTENT LAST, because content is the only one a frozen mirror can satisfy.

    Everything device-touching is behind IDeviceGateway, and the default implementation REFUSES rather
    than pretending: the rig is held by another lane, and a gateway that quietly returned success would
    manufacture exactly the green this project exists to prevent.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harness.Results\Harness.Results.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
